IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `wcima-compensation`

-- Workers Compensation and Injury Management Act 2023 (WA), ss 6, 12, 13, 17, 19, 20, 46-57, 69-78, 97-101, 186, 202, 204, 215, 415-424, 434 -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_workers-compensation-and-injury-management-act-2023.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

-- Scenario facts used (workbench scenarios/au/wa/cradle-to-grave-jake and -daniel facts.json and SCENARIO.md): Jake rides an
-- e-bike for a delivery platform on an ABN as a sole trader (2027-2034); on 2029-04-12 a car door breaks his wrist on a delivery
-- (k044). From 2034 he is employed by Sentinel Security Services Pty Ltd, which posts him to the tower where Jarrah is a tenant;
-- on 2053-10-05 he falls on a wet stairwell on patrol, is off eleven weeks, and is assessed at 14% whole person impairment (k085,
-- d080). Jarrah takes on three employees on 2031-06-01 (d044). The scenarios give no earnings: the $1,500 pre-injury weekly
-- rate and the $4,000 maximum weekly rate below are ILLUSTRATIVE inputs, not figures from the Act or the scenario. Whether
-- Jake's riding was a trade or business he regularly carried on in his own name (s 12(2)(c)(i)) is not stated; the k044 fixture
-- assumes it was (an ABN, his own tax return as a sole trader), and the opposite case is asserted too. The general maximum
-- amount is the s 538(1) figure, $243 991, unvaried by regulations.

